    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by elite speed and favorable matchups against mid-tier arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (79.12) commands the highest score of the day, capitalizing on a +14% platoon boost against Luis Castillo and providing the essential stolen base floor we prioritize. Close behind are **Trea Turner** (74.57) and **Kyle Schwarber** (73.45), both of whom benefit from a high-upside matchup against Junk. **Junior Caminero** (70.15) remains a must-start, as his power profile against Young, paired with a clean order position at #3, keeps his projection firmly in the elite tier. While **Caleb Durbin** (67.03) holds a strong rating due to a favorable matchup against Mitch Bratt, managers must remain vigilant regarding the 30% rain risk hovering over his contest, which could compress his plate appearance total.\n\nDecisions in the middle of our order required significant nuance today. **Colt Keith** (60.53) gets the nod over potential utility options due to the compounding benefits of hitting cleanup against Mlodzinski and a strong platoon outlook. The closest call for the final utility spot was **Carson Benge** (58.64); while his score fell just shy of the \"Strong\" threshold against Walker Buehler, he maintained the spot over bench depth like **Nelson Velazquez** and **Casey Schmitt** due to his projected order stability. We are unfortunately sidelined by scheduled off-days for core producers **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Gary Sanchez**, forcing us to rely on our active depth. With **Lars Nootbaar** (50.12) pending a confirmed lineup, we remain cautious; should he drop down the order or be scratched due to the aforementioned weather concerns, we have **Josh Smith** and **Hector Rodriguez** ready to rotate in to maintain our 5x5 coverage.",
